---
slug: admin/support/settings
layout: modules/support/agent
metadata:
  title: Support settings
---
{%- comment -%}
  Settings. A controller, like the queue: it gathers everything and hands
  finished arrays to the partials.

  Every write is its own small form posting to its own endpoint, so each
  one works with JavaScript off. The script only submits selects on
  change and copies the endpoint URL.

  The webhook secret is not rendered unless ?reveal=1 asks for it. That
  keeps it out of the page source, out of a screen share and out of a
  screenshot of this page, which is the usual way a shared secret leaks.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  # platformos-check-disable DeprecatedTag
  include 'modules/support/helpers/require_permission', do: 'support.settings.manage', entity: null
  # platformos-check-enable DeprecatedTag

  function current_profile = 'modules/user/helpers/current_profile'
  function settings = 'modules/support/queries/settings/get'
  function tokens = 'modules/support/helpers/ui/tokens'
  function departments = 'modules/support/queries/departments/all'
  function statuses = 'modules/support/queries/statuses/search', kind: null
  function all_agents = 'modules/support/queries/agents/all'
  function last_inbound = 'modules/support/queries/messages/last_inbound'
  function blocklist = 'modules/support/queries/blocked_senders/all', limit: 200

  assign brand = settings.brand_name | default: 'Support'

  comment
    A failed save flashes the first error and comes back with the row it
    was editing named in the query string, so the screen reopens where the
    admin was rather than collapsed with a message about a form they can
    no longer see.
  endcomment
  assign open_department = context.params.department
  assign reveal = false
  if context.params.reveal == '1'
    assign reveal = true
  endif

  comment
    Colour departments and agents by position, the same way the queue
    does, so a department is the same colour on every screen.
  endcomment
  assign palette_size = tokens.department_palette | size
  assign prepared_departments = []
  for department in departments
    assign palette_index = forloop.index0 | modulo: palette_size
    assign department.palette = tokens.department_palette[palette_index]
    assign department.letter = department.name | slice: 0, 1 | upcase
    assign department.is_open = false
    if open_department == department.id
      assign department.is_open = true
    endif
    assign prepared_departments = prepared_departments | array_add: department
  endfor

  assign agent_palette_size = tokens.agent_palette | size
  assign prepared_agents = []
  for agent in all_agents
    assign palette_index = forloop.index0 | modulo: agent_palette_size
    assign agent.palette = tokens.agent_palette[palette_index]
    assign prepared_agents = prepared_agents | array_add: agent
  endfor

  assign prepared_statuses = []
  for status in statuses
    assign token = tokens.statuses[status.key] | default: tokens.status_fallback
    assign status.token = token
    assign prepared_statuses = prepared_statuses | array_add: status
  endfor

  comment
    The one honest proof the inbound side works. A provider can be
    selected, keyed and still delivering nothing.
  endcomment
  assign inbound_at = last_inbound.created_at
  assign endpoint_base = 'https://' | append: context.location.host | append: '/support/inbound/sendgrid/'
  assign secret_mask = '••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••'

  assign endpoint_url = endpoint_base | append: secret_mask
  assign secret_display = secret_mask
  if reveal
    assign endpoint_url = endpoint_base | append: settings.webhook_secret
    assign secret_display = settings.webhook_secret
  endif
-%}
{% render 'modules/support/settings/nav', brand: brand, tokens: tokens, current_profile: current_profile %}
<main class="pos-support-main pos-support-settings">
  <header class="pos-support-settings-head">
    <h1>{{ 'modules/support/settings.title' | t }}</h1>
    <span>{{ 'modules/support/settings.subtitle' | t }}</span>
  </header>

  {% render 'modules/support/settings/departments', departments: prepared_departments %}
  {% render 'modules/support/settings/statuses', statuses: prepared_statuses %}
  {% render 'modules/support/settings/agents', agents: prepared_agents, departments: prepared_departments %}
  {% render 'modules/support/settings/email',
    settings: settings,
    inbound_at: inbound_at,
    endpoint_url: endpoint_url,
    secret_display: secret_display,
    reveal: reveal
  %}
  {% render 'modules/support/settings/blocklist', blocklist: blocklist %}
</main>
